Short answer: only partly. Under our conditions of carriage (version terms-2026-08):

- Vehicle bookings cancelled **at least 24 hours before departure** get a **full refund**.
- Cancellations made **less than 24 hours before departure** are refunded at **50%**.

Your sailing is tomorrow morning, so you are inside the 24-hour window if you cancel now. You would receive about half the fare back.

If you can change the sailing instead of cancelling, that is free up to 24 hours before departure. Changing it to a date at least 24 hours out would avoid the 50% refund. Otherwise, you can cancel now for the 50% refund.
